  "submitted_text": "Step 1: Given that \\( n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} \\), we can express \\( n \\) as \\( n = 7k + 2 \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\( n = 2 \\) into the expression \\((n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6)\\):\n\\[\n(n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6) = (2 + 2)(2 + 4)(2 + 6)\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Simplify the expression:\n\\[\n(2 + 2)(2 + 4)(2 + 6) = 4 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 8\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate the product:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 6 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\n24 \\cdot 8 = 192\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Find the remainder when 192 is divided by 7:\n\\[\n192 \\div 7 = 27 \\text{ remainder } 3\n\\]\nThus, \\( 192 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7} \\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{3}",
